tatus="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NOF CORP</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>UJIKAWA NORIHISA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HAYASHI, MASAKI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKAMURA, TOMOYUKI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NOF CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>UJIKAWA, NORIHISA</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HAYASHI MASAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAKAMURA TOMOYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>UJIKAWA NORIHISA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HAYASHI, MASAKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKAMURA, TOMOYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>UJIKAWA, NORIHISA</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A vinylated alkoxyamine represented by general formula (1) is produced by a process comprising the step of heating divinylbenzene together with a nitroxide compound and an organic peroxide to the heat decomposition temperature of the organic peroxide. In said formula, R&lt;1&gt; represents aryl or R&lt;2&gt;O; R&lt;2&gt; represents C1-12, linear or branched (cyclo)alkyl; and R&lt;3&gt; and R&lt;4&gt; each represents C4-6 tertiary alkyl or R&lt;3&gt; is bonded to R&lt;4&gt; to form a C8-16 cyclic structure which is unsubsituted or substituted by any of aklyl, oxo, hydroxy, acyloxy, and alkoxy. A polymeric free-radical polymerization initiator having a pendant alkoxyamine group can be used to produce a graft polymer.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>La présente invention concerne un alcoxyamine vinylé représenté par la formule générale (1), produit par un procédé consistant à chauffer du divinylbenzène avec un composé nitroxyde et un péroxyde organique jusqu'à la température de décomposition par la chaleur du péroxyde organique. Dans cette formule, R&lt;1&gt; représente aryle ou R&lt;2&gt;O; R&lt;2&gt; représente C1-12, (cyclo)alkyle linéaire ou ramifié; et R&lt;3&gt; et R&lt;4&gt; représentent chacun C4-6 alkyle tertiaire ou R&lt;3&gt; est lié à R&lt;4&gt; pour former une structure cyclique C8-16 non substituée ou substituée par alkyle, oxo, hydroxy, acyloxy, ou alcoxy. Par ailleurs, un amorceur de polymérisation à radicaux libres présentant un groupe alcoxyamine latéral peut être utilisé pour produire un polymère greffé.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>